{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/104334-trinity-time-line-and-recent-history","id":104334,"title":"Trinity Time Line and Recent History","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-02T14:21:45-07:00","id":104334,"title":"Trinity Time Line and Recent History","content":"Basically, my question is will the timeline of Aberrent by shifted to allow the events of more resent history to take place before the Galetea explosion or will the same general structure of the timeline remain the same? Specifically, will the timeline be adjusted to account for 9/11 and its own effects on history?<br /> <br /> Many people I know, including myself, find that fictional alternate Earth timelines that take place in the present or near future but diverge but diverge strongly from our own in the recent past create something of a shock, and can damage suspension of disbelief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T14:39:11-07:00","id":104345,"title":"","content":"The <b>Trinity Continuum</b> core book is going to feature a modern-day setting dealing with Talents and having an action movie feel to it. This strongly implies that the events of <b>Trinity Continuum: Aberrant</b> haven\u2019t happened yet.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Think of it this way: you know how the World of Darkness resembles our world, except that there are monsters hiding in the shadows? The core book\u2019s setting here will resemble our world too, but with an added helping of <i>awesome!</i> So don\u2019t worry about it diverging in any noticeable way from our recent past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-02-2014, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T18:56:27-07:00","id":104521,"title":"","content":"While worded as a concern, which to an extent it is as it probably would affect my enjoyment of the game, the intent is to spark a certain degree of discussion. I've seen some discussion of Talents, but nothing to specific as to their place in the timeline. If the modern setting is Talents that certainly takes care for timeline associated fears.<br /> <br /> It does present a question concerning Aberrant's place in the setting. Super hero settings tend to work best set in the present or near future. If we assume this to be true again for Aberrant that suggests our modern setting will be short lived and quickly give way to the Aberrant setting as the Galetea explosion happens in a few years. Give the world ten years again to adjust to the existence of Novas, and suddenly our start date for the Aberrant setting becomes the mid to late 2020's. That puts us withing 20 years of the Aberrant war, leaving two options, either the situation escalates quickly toward the Aberrant War or the whole time line gets shifted again pushing Aeon further into the future.<br /> <br /> This adjustment of the timeline also necessitates a change in the wonders that Novas bring to the world. Many of their early wonders we as normal humans are on the threshold of achieving. AIDS is being treated and likely on its way to be cured, which presents its own dilemma as AIDS is now being reprogrammed to train the immune system to effectively target cancers. Sexually transmitted cancer immunity could be in the near future. In light of our own technological advancements over the past decade and a half, what Novas do for the world must be reexamined.<br /> <br /> Just food for thought. Also I love feeding discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T20:14:17-07:00","id":104553,"title":"","content":"So Aberrant will always be like 10 years in the future?<br /> <br /> Were Talents something from Adventure or were they something new for the Corebook?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T20:42:28-07:00","id":104563,"title":"","content":"Hark: there\u2019s also the possibility of narrowing the gap between the Aberrant War and the \u00c6on setting. <br /> <br /> Eldagusto: Talents are based on Adventure!\u2019s daredevils. Presumably, they\u2019re being featured in the core rulebook because they can be found in all eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T20:58:01-07:00","id":104571,"title":"","content":"Well I'm glad we are getting one corebook. I always liked that approach, it was always a pain for me to buy/read the same information over and over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T08:41:56-07:00","id":104851,"title":"","content":"Amen. I loved it when the nWoD did a system core and then did line books. This is great to save on wordcount for the line books to include either more setting or more crunch. Either way, it benefits things in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T09:33:49-07:00","id":104884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/104334-trinity-time-line-and-recent-history?p=104563#post104563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hark: there\u2019s also the possibility of narrowing the gap between the Aberrant War and the \u00c6on setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew there was something wrong when I planned for three possibilities before writing the post, and when I went to write it could only think of two. Though that options makes Aeon much more of a post apocalypses setting and less a space opera setting if my understanding of the Aberrant War is correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T10:33:35-07:00","id":104922,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily, Hark.<br /> <br /> As currently written, the Aberrant War ends in 2061, with the Trinity setting beginning in 2120. That's 59 years. For comparison, 59 years ago was 1955, the year the Vietnam War started.<br /> <br /> Assuming the new edition of Aeon also starts in 2120, what if we nudge the end of the Aberrant War forward to 2070? That still allows a solid 50 years for recovery (modern comparison: 1964, the year of the Gulf of Tonkin incident, bringing the US into the Vietnam War). 50 years still seems perfectly reasonable to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T16:01:21-07:00","id":105153,"title":"","content":"As I said, the assumption is based off my understanding of the Aberrant War which very well could be flawed in the apocalyptic scale I understand it to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:31:17-07:00","id":106408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/104334-trinity-time-line-and-recent-history?p=104922#post104922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily, Hark.<br /> <br /> As currently written, the Aberrant War ends in 2061, with the Trinity setting beginning in 2120. That's 59 years. For comparison, 59 years ago was 1955, the year the Vietnam War started.<br /> <br /> Assuming the new edition of Aeon also starts in 2120, what if we nudge the end of the Aberrant War forward to 2070? That still allows a solid 50 years for recovery (modern comparison: 1964, the year of the Gulf of Tonkin incident, bringing the US into the Vietnam War). 50 years still seems perfectly reasonable to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That only narrows the time between the war by nine years which is trivial, but the problem is that it is only a nine year shift to compensate for something in the area of thirty or so years shift in the time on the other side of the war if the setting is shifted for both the real world time and the insertion of a new period.<br /> <br /> First there is the shift of about 17 years (I forget the exact year the explosion at the moment) to the real-world now assuming that the satellite explosion has to happen sometime after near or after the current time to allow for the Corebook setting. Then there is the length of time the setting in the Core book lasts assuming that it extends into the future at all rather than a near historic projection that ends with the explosion and the dawn of the Nova/Aberrant age in the real world \u201cnow\u201d (though there is no reason it could not overlap a bit either).<br /> <br /> Then from the explosion there is the ramp up to the tip-over point (and the \u201cnow\u201d of the Aberrant game) which in the first edition was about ten years (which if anything seemed a bit rushed as it was). The ramp-up time could be shaved down if the \u201cGolden Age\u201d is eliminated and things turn nasty almost right away, but that would make it mock the comics (which some sci-fi/horror stories do) instead of contrast with them (personally I prefer the contrast approach but both are valid). Things could fall apart faster than the original after the tipping point as well to absorb some of the extra time but it can only go so far in that regard before seeming like a deus ex machine end to the Nova era.<br /> <br /> This assumes that the Corebook setting is strictly contemporary and completely free of Nova influence. If it is something more like the \u201cAgents of S.H.I.E.L.D.\u201d type setting where there is some Nova action going on in the background distracting the public but not really the focus of the setting the explosion could be as early as 2005 if the start of the Aberrant \u201ccurrent time\u201d is 2015. Having both meet at the \u201ccurrent time\u201d from different directions and overlap a bit would probably be the most compact way of doing it so the war and the Trinity era would not have to be pushed as much if at all.<br /> <br /> Of course there are some people who would object to a massively different \u201cnow\u201d that would be in line with the changes seen in the Aberrant \u201cnow\u201d so having the explosion be close to the real-world &quot;now&quot; and putting the Aberrant &quot;now&quot; in the near future like the original might still be the best way to go despite the shifts it would cause in the later eras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}